      "id": "fYBKw",
      "text": "Mole fraction",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Molarity<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>No. of  Moles of solute </mtext><mtext> Volume of solution in L </mtext></mfrac></math></p><p>Since volume depends on temperature, molarity will change upon change in temperature.</p><p>As the temperature rises, the volume of the solution increases. When the temperature increases the molarity of the solution will decrease as temperature depends on volume.</p><p>Hence option A is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
